url: https://github.com/uedaLabR/rnaModScan
license: MIT
abstract: rnaModScan filters nanopore direct RNA sequencing modification calls using Dorado modification
  scores, local sequence and read features. A shared neural classifier distinguishes m6A, inosine and
  false-positive candidates; m5C and pseudouridine have auxiliary reference- and motif-based reporting.
  The source archive includes dependency specifications, CPU/GPU Docker build files, prepared human reference
  maps with provenance, mouse RMBase source archives, the HEK293T evaluation checkpoint used for the manuscript's
  HeLa analyses, and a separate pooled HEK293T/HeLa deployment model. The supplied checkpoints require
  the documented TensorFlow 2.10.1/Keras 2.10.0 runtime. Third-party reference data retain their original
  terms and attribution; the software MIT License does not relicense those datasets.
keywords:
- RNA modifications
- nanopore direct RNA sequencing
- m6A
- inosine
- deep learning
- bioinformatics
